# The migration files are hashed into the migration ledger, so the bytes
# of a migration have to mean the same thing on every machine.  A
# checkout that rewrites the line endings of the file changes the bytes
# of a migration that has already run, and the migration tool then
# refuses to apply the migrations that are still pending.  The migration
# tool normalizes the line endings before it hashes the text as well, so
# the two rules together make the ledger independent of the checkout.
flashloan/tools/manager_db/migrations/*.sql text eol=lf
